# gorget-js snag #15c — the multi-statement sibling of snag #15b.
#
# Post-Track-F (snag #15b, single-expression bodies): `gg fmt` still wrapped
# MULTI-STATEMENT `else:` / `catch (e):` / `rethrow (e):` bodies in a
# spurious `do:` block. Not breaking (the output compiles + preserves
# behavior) but a readability regression + rot magnet (users read the
# reformatted `catch (e): do:` and re-add the `do:` on rewrites, then hit
# snag #15b when they simplify to a single-expression body).
#
# 16 sites in gorget-js: main.gg 9, parser.gg 5, eval.gg 2.
#
# RETIRED R39 Track G (2026-08-09) by extending `format_arm_body` at
# `src/formatter/mod.rs:1174+` to also handle `Expr::Do { body }` — the
# parser wraps indented catch/rethrow bodies as `Expr::Do` via
# `parse_body_or_expr`, not `Expr::Block`. Track F only covered the
# `Expr::Block` single-`Stmt::Expr` case.
#
# The fix now recognizes BOTH ast forms (Expr::Block from match `else:`
# via `parse_arm_body`, Expr::Do from catch/rethrow via
# `parse_body_or_expr`) and emits bare-indented-block for multi-stmt +
# inline for single-expression, no `do:` re-emission at any of the three
# arm sites.
int compute(int x) throws String:
    if x < 0:
        throw "negative"
    return x * 2

int safe(int x):
    int r = compute(x)! catch (e):
        print("recovering")
        0
    return r

int main():
    print(safe(5))
    print(safe(-1))
    return 0
